<title>JAPAN: Japan average rates on time deposits.</title>
<headline>Japan average rates on time deposits.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Average rates on time deposits of more than 10 million yen in the week to April 9 as released by the Bank of Japan on Wednesday:</p>
<p>    one mth	0.34 (0.34)	 one year     0.37 (0.37)</p>
<p>    three mths   0.34 (0.34)	 two years    0.48 (0.49)</p>
<p>    six mths     0.35 (0.35)	 three years  0.93 (0.94)</p>
<p>Average rates on time deposits of three to 10 million yen:</p>
<p>    one mth	0.30 (0.30)	 one year     0.32 (0.32)</p>
<p>    three mths   0.30 (0.30)	 two years    0.43 (0.44)</p>
<p>    six mths     0.30 (0.30)	 three years  0.88 (0.89)</p>
<p>Average rates on time deposits of less than three million</p>
<p>yen:</p>
<p>    one mth	0.25 (0.25)	 one year     0.28 (0.28)</p>
<p>    three mths   0.25 (0.25)	 two years    0.38 (0.39)</p>
<p>    six mths     0.25 (0.25)	 three years  0.83 (0.84)</p>
<p>Average rates on certificates of deposit, Apr 07 - Apr 11:</p>
<p>    less than 30 days  0.53 (0.58)   120-150 days  0.57 (0.56)</p>
<p>    30-60 days	   0.56 (0.57)   150-180 days  0.59 (0.57)</p>
<p>    60-90 days	   0.55 (0.56)   180-360 days  0.58 (0.65)</p>
<p>    90-120 days	  0.55 (0.56)   over 360 days 0.61 (0.68)</p>
</text>
